  "youtube": {
    "title": "They Liked You More Than You Think #shorts",
    "description": "That conversation you keep replaying at 2 a.m.? The other person is probably replaying it too, and smiling.\n\nPsychologists call it the liking gap: after talking with someone new, people consistently underestimate how much the other person liked them. You notice every awkward second of your own. They mostly don't.\n\nSo text them first.\n\nResearch: Boothby, Cooney, Sandstrom & Clark (2018), \"The Liking Gap in Conversations\", Psychological Science.\n\n#shorts #psychology #overthinking #socialanxiety #friendship #animation #selfimprovement",
